# Copy to api/.env (git-ignored) to set these without typing them each time.

# An Anthropic API key from console.anthropic.com. With it, lawyers can also choose Claude for a
# review (a real API call, paid per review) with the switch in the app; the simulated AI stays the
# default. Without it, only the simulated AI is offered. The API checks for it at startup.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Claude's settings are "claudeReviewer" in config.json; these override them for this machine.
# Shown with the values in config.json (the smallest, cheapest model):
# REVIEWER_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# REVIEWER_EFFORT=low
# REVIEWER_THINKING=off
# Hard limit on the tokens one review may use, input and output over all its turns:
# REVIEWER_TOKEN_BUDGET=30000

# The rules and timings (the 60-second deadline, 1,000 reviews a month, the session lifetime, the
# fake AI's timings) are in config.json. To try other values, copy it and point here to the copy
# (a relative path starts from api/):
# CONFIG_FILE=config.demo.json
